00:02:49,411 --> 00:02:55,411
Captain Phillips is a 2013 American biographical
action-thriller film directed by Paul Greengrass.

9
00:03:10,588 --> 00:03:16,588
Based on the 2009 Maersk Alabama hijacking, the film tells the story of Captain Richard
Phillips, an American merchant mariner who was taken hostage by Somali pirates.

10
00:03:31,764 --> 00:03:37,764
It stars Tom Hanks as Phillips, alongside Barkhad
Abdi as pirate leader Abduwali Muse.

11
00:03:52,941 --> 00:03:58,941
The screenplay by Billy Ray is based on Phillips's 2010 book A Captain's Duty: Somali Pirates,
Navy SEALs, and Dangerous Days at Sea, which Phillips co-wrote with Stephan Talty.

12
00:04:14,117 --> 00:04:20,117
Scott Rudin, Dana Brunetti and Michael De Luca
served as producers on the project.

13
00:04:35,294 --> 00:04:41,294
It premiered at the 2013 New York Film Festival, and was
theatrically released on October 11, 2013.

14
00:04:56,470 --> 00:05:02,470
The film emerged as a critical and commercial success, receiving acclaim from
critics and grossing $218 million against a budget of $55 million.

15
00:05:17,647 --> 00:05:23,647
Captain Phillips received six Academy Award nominations, including Best
Picture, Best Adapted Screenplay and Best Supporting Actor for Abdi.

16
00:05:38,823 --> 00:05:44,823
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
